# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY reverse map for the login-ui Tier-1 overlay.
#
# These are the ORIGINAL literal values that the 4 brand-coupled tokens carry in
# the READ-ONLY upstream base (snapdragon-login-ui @ Snapdragon-Systems). They
# are NOT secrets and NOT tenant brand — they are the base's own identity.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders the overlay with EXACTLY these
# values and asserts the result is byte-identical to a freshly-pulled base. If
# the base drifts in any of the 4 overlaid files (a non-templated line changed,
# or a templated line's surrounding context moved), that byte-compare breaks and
# the validator fails loudly (patch-reject + overlayed-region checksum). This is
# how the overlay stays honest without ever vendoring the base into the generator.
#
# NOT consumed by the renderer at emit time — render_repo_tree.sh derives the
# REAL tenant values from the brand profile. This file is the drift oracle only.
#
# Shell-sourced KEY=VALUE (same idiom as brands/*.conf).
BRAND_TITLE="Snapdragon Login (remote)"
NPM_SCOPE="snapdragon"
HOST_NAME="snapdragon-host"
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="Snapdragon-Systems/snapdragon-generator"
